+# Test report — FluxVM Secure Containers Set 3
+
+## Base verification
+
+GitHub main was re-checked during this handoff. The latest reviewed base was
+`d77c1afb9364b02e897079b7325470e9a2bf361e`, after the Set 2 merge and three
+runtime fixes for stdio, virtiofs share mounting, and i64 exit timestamps.
+
+## Checks executed in the artifact environment
+
+- shell syntax validation with `bash -n`
+- TOML parsing for every `Cargo.toml`
+- YAML parsing for deployment manifests
+- Rust delimiter/lexical balance checks for all new Rust sources
+- protocol/request/response consistency review
+- source-level comparison with current containerd `rust-extensions` task-event
+  and `RemotePublisher` APIs
+- archive integrity and SHA-256 verification
+
+## Not executable in this environment
+
+The artifact container does not provide `rustc`/`cargo`, `/dev/kvm`, QEMU or a
+running containerd. Therefore this report does **not** claim Rust compilation,
+clippy success, VM boot, ctr execution or Kubernetes E2E success here.
+
+## Required merge gate
+
+Before production use, run the repository CI plus a Linux KVM node test that
+covers create/start/wait/delete, exec, pause/resume, kill, TaskExit events,
+Stats/Pids/Update, Pod CNI connectivity, teardown, and repeated Pod churn.
